messages:
zoe_product: quick heads-up from today's a11y lab — dense Models table still has a weird 'focus-ring stutter' when tabbing fast on Windows+Chrome. NVDA sometimes reads the previous row then the current row (double announce).

liam_ui: thanks Zoe. I can repro locally. If I tab quickly the outline appears then briefly reappears on the previous row for a frame. Only happens in Compact density.

rachel_a11y: repro steps and environment pls? NVDA + Chrome / JAWS? need to know SR text sequence.

zoe_product: repro: Console -> Models -> Density: Compact -> Tab through rows quickly (20+ tabs). Windows 10, Chrome 118, NVDA 2024.2. NVDA reads: "Model X, selected" then "Model Y, selected" but sometimes says "Model X" again as if focus bounced.

liam_ui: I think two things are colliding: 1) we have tabindex=0 on the row container and also on a hidden focusable badge node inside some cells; 2) we animate a shadow on :focus which triggers a paint and may reflow in some GPUs.

rachel_a11y: if there are duplicate focusable nodes you will definitely get double announcements. Also animated paint/reflow can cause screen readers to re-scan. Let's ensure single logical focus per row. Two suggested strategies: a) make only the row tabbable (tabindex=0) and mark inner elements aria-hidden or remove tabindex, b) keep row index-only but use <div role="row"> and cells role="gridcell" so SR announces row-level content predictably.

liam_ui: plan: audit DOM, remove tabindex from non-interactive children, and scope visual hover animations to :hover only. For keyboard focus use :focus-visible so mouse hover still has scale. Example CSS patch:
```css
/* keyboard focus is simple and high-contrast */
.models-row:focus-visible {
  transform: none; /* no scale on keyboard */
  box-shadow: none;
  border: 2px solid var(--focus-accent);
  border-radius: 6px;
  outline: none;
}
/* keep subtle hover for mouse users */
.models-row:hover {
  transform: scale(1.02);
  transition: transform 120ms ease;
}
```

zoe_product: good. Also the status badge updates (Queued -> Training) currently use a visual-only dot. SR users don't hear that. Could we add an aria-live region on the status text?

rachel_a11y: yes: non-critical state changes should be polite. Example markup suggestion: `<span class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Status: Training</span>`. Ensure the text is present in DOM (not only via background-image) so SR reads it.

liam_ui: noted. We'll update the badge component to include accessible text and role=status. Also will avoid toggling tabindex on that node.

frank_sre: small note — the skip-to-main link currently goes to `#models-table` but the sticky header covers it on smaller viewports. We should add `html { scroll-padding-top: var(--site-header-height); }` or `:target { scroll-margin-top: var(--site-header-height); }`. This keeps the first row visible.

rachel_a11y: agree. Also add an automated Lighthouse check for skiplink landing. And add an axe rule alerting for duplicate tabbable nodes inside rows.

a11y_bot: created ticket A11Y-223: Dense models table 1 focus stutter, duplicate tabbable nodes, missing aria-live. Suggested tests: axe-core CI, puppeteer keyboard tab-sequence test, cross-browser NVDA/VoiceOver manual pass.

liam_ui: I'll open a small PR today: 1) DOM audit to remove extra tabindex, 2) CSS switch to :focus-visible and remove transform on keyboard, 3) update badge markup with role=status.

zoe_product: thanks 1 can you include a quick test script in the PR description for QA? e.g., steps to reproduce with NVDA and to verify no double read and single focus ring.

rachel_a11y: will add the manual test steps and run NVDA/VoiceOver on staging after PR. If we still see double announces we'll capture a screen recording and file a SxS with Chrome devtools paint profiler.

liam_ui: tagging @frank_sre for the scroll-padding change in case there are edge cases with dynamic header height during deploy.

frank_sre: will review. If we use CSS variables for header height and update them on breakpoint JS, should be fine.

zoe_product: timeline? this looks like a release-blocker for making Compact default.

liam_ui: aiming to land the PR by EOD, get a11y review tomorrow morning. If all green we'll ship in next patch.

rachel_a11y: thanks team. I'll run the SR passes and report back. :white_check_mark:
